          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why did Turbo Pascal compile units into .TPU files?",
          "options": [
            "So they didn't have to be compiled again every time",
            "To hide them",
            "To make them smaller on screen",
            "To print them"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only the program you changed was compiled again: much faster."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p19-l2",
      "title": "Interface and Implementation",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Everything in the implementation that isn't in the interface is private. A program that uses the unit can't see it, so it can't break it by accident.",
        "In the example, the variable n is only in the implementation. The program can call Tick and Count, but writing n := 100 in the program gives Error 3: Unknown identifier.",
        "This is called information hiding. You can change how a unit works inside, and every program using it keeps working, as long as the interface stays the same."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "unit Counter;",
          "",
          "interface",
          "",
          "procedure Tick;",
          "function Count: integer;",
          "",
          "implementation",
          "",
          "var",
          "  n: integer; { private: only this unit can see it }",
          "",
          "procedure Tick;",
          "begin",
          "  n := n + 1;",
          "end;",
          "",
          "function Count: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  Count := n;",
          "end;",
          "",
          "end.",
          "",
          "program Clicks;",
          "uses Counter;",
          "var",
          "  i: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  for i := 1 to 3 do",
          "    Tick;",
          "  writeln('Ticks: ', Count);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Ticks: 3"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "The variable n is declared only in the implementation. Who can use it?",
          "options": [
            "Only the routines in the unit",
            "Every program using the unit",
            "Nobody",
            "Only the main program"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only what's in the interface is visible outside."
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e2",
          "type": "find_bug",
