            "  Tick;",
            "  n := 100;",
            "  writeln(Count);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 28,
          "explanation": "n is private to the unit: Unknown identifier. The program can only use Tick and Count."
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e3",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why hide things in the implementation?",
          "options": [
            "Programs can't break them, and the inside can change without breaking programs",
            "It makes the program faster",
            "Pascal doesn't allow public variables",
            "To save memory"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "That's information hiding."
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e4",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Make Reset usable from programs.",
          "code": [
            "interface",
            "",
            "procedure Tick;",
            "procedure ___;",
            "",
            "implementation"
          ],
          "options": [
            "Reset",
            "Tick",
            "Count",
            "begin"
          ],
          "answer": "Reset",
          "explanation": "A heading in the interface makes the routine public."
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the implementation, Turbo Pascal allowed procedure Tick; without the parameters again. Why?",
          "options": [
            "The interface already gave the full heading",
            "Tick has no parameters anyway",
            "It's a mistake",
            "The parameters are private"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Both short and full headings were accepted."
        },
        {
          "id": "p19-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does this program print?",
          "code": [
            "unit Counter;",
            "",
            "interface",
            "",
            "procedure Tick;",
